WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.981
This episode focuses on end-to-end practice.

2
00:00:03.981 --> 00:00:11.667
Census data becomes useful when the population, measure, geography, and time period are stated before anyone searches for a number.

3
00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:19.706
A defensible workflow begins with a written question, decision owner, population, measure, geography, period, and acceptable uncertainty.

4
00:00:19.706 --> 00:00:24.929
It then selects the Census program and the local primary source for their distinct roles.

5
00:00:24.929 --> 00:00:34.164
Create a source register with titles, publishers, URLs, vintages, table or variable identifiers, universes, geographic codes, and retrieval dates.

6
00:00:34.164 --> 00:00:37.706
Save raw downloads and API requests before calculations.

7
00:00:37.706 --> 00:00:43.267
Check margins of error, product compatibility, boundary changes, inflation, and disclosure constraints.

8
00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:50.178
Record every transformation and preserve a dated interpretation that distinguishes evidence from assumptions and adopted policy.

9
00:00:50.178 --> 00:00:51.953
Torrance application segment.

10
00:00:51.953 --> 00:00:56.297
This local application is separate from the Census Academy instruction.

11
00:00:56.297 --> 00:01:05.354
The cited City of Torrance primary source is City of Torrance primary-source set, published at https://www.torranceca.gov/Government/About-Torrance.

12
00:01:05.354 --> 00:01:18.205
For a local analysis, assemble the About Torrance, General Plan, housing, transportation-analysis, and audit pages as separately labeled local records, then pair each claim with the appropriate federal dataset.

13
00:01:18.205 --> 00:01:26.833
Do not present City policy or administrative records as Census Bureau findings, and do not present a federal estimate as adopted City policy.

14
00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:36.451
Keep a reproducibility packet containing the question, source URLs, exact vintage, table or query, geography codes, raw result, calculations, and uncertainty note.

15
00:01:36.451 --> 00:01:39.579
This narration is an original synthesis of cited U.S.

16
00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:44.181
Census Bureau government works and separately cited City of Torrance material.

17
00:01:44.181 --> 00:01:48.312
Third-party videos, software, graphics, and linked works are excluded.

18
00:01:48.312 --> 00:01:54.094
This product uses Census Bureau information but is not endorsed or certified by the Census Bureau.

19
00:01:54.094 --> 00:01:58.284
It is not an official City product and does not imply City endorsement.
